course: dictionary
lesson: 7396
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context tells you which meaning the writer means. Poacher has three meanings: a person who hunts animals illegally, a pan for gently cooking eggs, and a sports player who waits near the goal to score.
explain: «Poachers kill elephants for their tusks, and selling ivory is banned in most countries.» The words tusks, ivory and banned show this is about illegal hunting, so poacher means a person who hunts or catches animals illegally.
explain: «Pass me the poacher, I want to cook the eggs gently.» Here there are no animals and no hunting. Cooking and eggs are the clues, so poacher means a pan. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A poacher is a person who hunts or catches animals illegally, often rare animals like elephants and rhinos.
fact: In sport, a poacher is a player who scores by waiting near the goal.
fact: A poacher can also be a pan for poaching, which means gently cooking eggs.
fact: «Rhino horn is made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and fingernails», so it is no medicine, though some people wrongly think it is.
fact: A word with several meanings is picked by its context: the words around it show which meaning is right.
exercise: «Dian Fossey fought against poachers who trapped mountain gorillas in Rwanda.» What does poacher mean here? | A player who scores near the goal | A park ranger who guards the forest | A pan for gently cooking eggs | *A person who hunts or catches animals illegally
exercise: Dad says, «Pass me the poacher, I'll cook the eggs gently.» What is a poacher here? | A person who hunts animals | A ranger in a national park | *A pan for gently cooking eggs | A goal scorer who waits near the goal
exercise: Sam waited near the goal all match and scored three times. What kind of player is Sam? | *A poacher | An ivory dealer | A gamekeeper | A ranger
test: «Rhino horn is made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and fingernails; it is no medicine, but people who wrongly think it is pay poachers who kill rhinos for it.» In this sentence, what does poacher mean? | A tourist who visits parks | *A person who kills animals illegally | A player who scores near the goal | A pan for cooking eggs
test: Mum cracked two eggs into the poacher and let them cook gently. Which meaning of poacher fits? | *A pan for gently cooking eggs | A person who hunts animals | A football striker | A park guard
exam: «In old stories, a poacher steals rabbits or deer from a rich landowner.» Which meaning fits, and which words show you why? | *A person who hunts animals illegally, because of steals, rabbits and deer | A rich landowner | A pan for cooking eggs | A player who scores goals
